print("Think slow")

<PROGRAM END>


The file contains 491438 bytes of text.

---

I'm using Windows 7 64 bit.

I'm editing the text in Notepad++ and it is encoded as utf-8.

I'm compiling with LuaJIT 2.0.5 beta.<issue_comment>username_1: The text is not displayed, because Lua prints a lot of garbage. You can see the full output by running `luajit -e "print('Think slow')"` instead in the command line (Windows).
Upvotes: 3 [selected_answer]<issue_comment>username_2: You can also run it via command prompt, just open cmd then type 


luajit filename.lua



if you are in the folder where your file is. If you want to run more than one file at once use `luajit -e "print('Think slow')"` or `luajit -e "print('This is a test')"`
